#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Recording One"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:38
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Where It Is Offered"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_public_archive.html.heex:57
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "/cs"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_public_archive.html.heex:42
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A busy day is split into pages of 200 lines, with Earlier and Later links between them"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_public_archive.html.heex:28
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Attachments are never published — the page only notes that one was there"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_public_archive.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The founder, and nobody else. An operator moderates the room; deciding that what is said in it becomes readable from outside is a different kind of decision, so it belongs to whoever answers for the channel. The switch is in Channel Central, on the Registration tab, or typed as /cs archive on and /cs archive off; only a registered channel has one."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_public_archive.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The founder must be identified with NickServ to switch it, not merely using the founder's nickname"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:33
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A recording stops by itself after one minute and is sent as it is. After a minute it stops being something the other person can take in during a conversation, which is what writing is for."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:40
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On a desktop and on a phone, in any browser that can record. If the browser cannot record, the microphone does not appear, and the attachment button can still send an audio file."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:21
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only the Recording Is Sent"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Press the microphone and allow access when the browser asks. While you speak, the recording replaces the input: a red dot, a clock that counts up, a button to discard it and a button to send it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Some things are faster said than typed. The microphone button sits in the toolbar beside the message input, next to the attachment and formatting buttons. It records up to a minute of audio and sends it as a separate message."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:15
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The send button ends the recording and sends it. The discard button deletes it. In both cases the microphone turns off."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_voice_messages.html.heex:24
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only the recording is sent. Text you typed stays in the input. Files waiting to be attached stay too."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_copy.html.heex:10
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "2. Open the Edit menu and choose Copy, or press %{keys}."
msgstr ""

